summary:
  The Edit dialog finds its row by address alone, so of two rows on one
  address it can take the other one.

history:
  A heal moved the row being edited off an address a second row also held,
  or a removal shifted the rows: the OK was written onto the other twin.
  The dialog prefers the row with the name it was opened with, which the
  popup never writes.

target:
  package/contents/ui/DoorLogic.js

find:
      var tries = [["hostname", true], ["prev", true]];

replace:
      var tries = [["hostname", false], ["prev", false]];

expect:
  Killed by tst_doorlogic::test_the_dialog_knows_its_twin_by_the_name_it_opened_with.
  Line-neutral.
